            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4918",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[GO-2026-4918] Infinite loop in HTTP/2 transport when given bad SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE in net/http/internal/http2 in golang.org/x/net"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Infinite loop in HTTP/2 transport when given bad SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE in net/http/internal/http2 in golang.org/x/net"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "When processing HTTP/2 SETTINGS frames, transport will enter an infinite loop of writing CONTINUATION frames if it receives a SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE with a value of 0."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-4918",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2026-33814"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-5025",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[GO-2026-5025] Invoking incorrect handling of namespaced elements in foreign content in golang.org/x/net/html"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Invoking incorrect handling of namespaced elements in foreign content in golang.org/x/net/html"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Parsing arbitrary HTML which is then rendered using Render can result in an unexpected HTML tree. This can be leveraged to execute XSS attacks in applications that attempt to sanitize input HTML before rendering."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-5025",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2026-42506"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-5026",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[GO-2026-5026] Invoking failure to reject ASCII-only Punycode-encoded labels in golang.org/x/net/idna"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Invoking failure to reject ASCII-only Punycode-encoded labels in golang.org/x/net/idna"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The ToASCII and ToUnicode functions incorrectly accept Punycode-encoded labels that decode to an ASCII-only label. For example, ToUnicode(\"xn--example-.com\") incorrectly returns the name \"example.com\" rather than an error.\n\nThis behavior can lead to privilege escalation in programs using the idna package. For example, a program which performs privilege checks on the ASCII hostname may reject \"example.com\" but permit \"xn--example-.com\". If that program subsequently converts the ASCII hostname to Unicode, it will inadvertently permits access to the Unicode name \"example.com\"."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-5026",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2026-39821"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-5027",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[GO-2026-5027] Invoking incorrect handling of HTML elements in foreign content in golang.org/x/net/html"
              },
